stalled and available in shell via `python3.x` commands.","     See Python installation tips in [Developer Wiki](https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/BEAM/Python+Tips#PythonTips-InstallingPythoninterpreters).","-  - If you encounter errors like `python3.10: command not found` or `Cannot run program \"python3.10\": No such file or directory`, your system may be missing some Python versions.","-    Workaround: install missing versions with `pyenv` (for example, `pyenv install 3.10` then `pyenv global 3.10 3.11 3.12 3.13` to make all available), or create symlinks in `/usr/local/bin/` pointing to installed Python binaries.","+  - If you encounter errors like `python3.11: command not found` or `Cannot run program \"python3.11\": No such file or directory`, your system may be missing some Python versions.","+    Workaround: install missing versions with `pyenv` (for example, `pyenv install 3.11` then `pyenv global 3.11 3.12 3.13 3.14` to make all available), or create symlinks in `/usr/local/bin/` pointing to installed Python binaries."," - For large contributions, a signed [Individual Contributor License","   Agreement](https://www.apache.org/licenses/icla.pdf) (ICLA) to the Apache","   Software Foundation (ASF)."],"additions":2,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"contributor-docs/python-tips.md","lines":["@@ -57,22 +57,22 @@ Installation steps may look as follows:"," 2. Install Python intepreter for each supported Python minor version. Leaving out the patch version will install the latest."," "," ```bash","-pyenv install 3.10"," pyenv install 3.11"," pyenv install 3.12"," pyenv install 3.13","+pyenv install 3.14"," ```"," "," 3. Make installed interpreters available in your shell by first running:"," "," ```bash","-pyenv global 3.10 3.11 3.12 3.13","+pyenv global 3.11 3.12 3.13 3.14"," ```"," "," 4. (**OPTIONAL**) Pyenv will sometimes [fail to make these interpreters directly available](https://github.com/pyenv/pyenv/issues/34) without a local configuratio